ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the A7 DrivesList / BatteryHealth precedents)
  EfficiencyPageModel.kt       framework-free: EfficiencyPageRegistration; the verbatim port of
                               the web getEfficiency + the efficiencyColor thresholds
                               (EfficiencyTier); the EfficiencyStats decode of the raw SI
                               /drives/stats JSON; EfficiencyDisplayPrefs (web useUnits/useSettings:
                               toDistance/toSpeed/toTemperature/toEfficiency + number/integer +
                               shared formatDuration/formatEnergy); the useMemo fold
                               (deriveEfficiencyData → dailyTrend / speedVsEfficiency /
                               tempVsEfficiency / speedDistribution / tempBuckets); costPerKm /
                               kmPerKwh / regenPercent / driveTimeMax; EfficiencyDateRange;
                               mapData; view.opened.
  EfficiencyPageSource.kt      seam over DrivingRepository.drives (web useDrives) +
                               DrivingRepository.drivingStats (web useDrivingStats) +
                               SettingsStore.settings + SelectedVehicleStore.
  EfficiencyPageViewModel.kt   BaseFeedViewModel; drivesState: StateFlow<UiState<List<Drive>>> +
                               statsState: StateFlow<UiState<EfficiencyStats>> both gated on the
                               active vehicle (web useSelectedVehicle / enabled:!!vehicleId);
                               displayPrefs StateFlow; dateRange + setDateRange (web from/to URL
                               cells, default last 30 days); refresh/retry; recordViewOpened.
  EfficiencyScatterChart.kt    Compose-native Canvas scatter (the A3 chart lib carries no scatter
                               wrapper — same Canvas approach as BatteryHealthPage's AC/DC pie;
                               never a webview) with min/mid/max axis ticks + axis names.
  EfficiencyPageIcons.kt       EfficiencyGlyphs (web lucide): Zap=DataDisplayGlyphs.Bolt,
                               Gauge=DataDisplayGlyphs.Gauge, TrendingUp/Thermometer/Fuel authored
                               locally as 24×24 stroked vectors.
  EfficiencyPage.kt            stateful entry + stateless content; loading/empty/error/success;
                               the hero gauge + 3 count-up tiles, the 4 stat cards + no-stats
                               panel, the daily-trend area chart, the speed-range bar chart, the
                               two scatter plots, the temperature-bucket table, the metric-bars
                               summary and the energy-insights grid; chrome = title/subtitle +
                               freshness chip + VehicleSelect (header picker) + DateRangeFilter +
                               stale banner.
  EfficiencyPageHost.kt        EfficiencyRoute + EfficiencyPageHost.register() for the
                               `efficiency` / `/efficiency` destination (Destinations.kt L73;
                               registered in TeslaSyncApplication.kt).

DATA SOURCES (each bound through the ViewModel's StateFlow over the KMP core, P1/S8)
  useDrives        → DrivingRepository.drives(vehicleId)        → drivesState
  useDrivingStats  → DrivingRepository.drivingStats(vehicleId)  → statsState (JsonElement → EfficiencyStats)
  The host builds HttpDrivingRepository(container.api, container.cacheStore) — the Android DI graph
  wires no DrivingStore, so the page-local repository reuses the shared resilient client + offline
  cache (ADR-013 freshness + SI-verbatim caching), exactly as the sibling DrivesList surface does.

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  Per-drive efficiency stays SI Wh/km, distance metres, speed m/s, temperature °C end to end.
  Display conversion happens only at the render boundary via EfficiencyDisplayPrefs.toDistance/
  toSpeed/toTemperature/toEfficiency (convertDistanceFromSI/convertSpeedFromSI/convertTempFromSI +
  the Wh/km→Wh/mi factor) and the shared formatDuration/formatEnergy. The `/drives/stats` figures
  (avgEfficiencyWhKm / totalDistanceKm / avgSpeedKmh / topSpeedKmh) are passed through the same
  converters the web page applies (toDistanceDisplay(stats.totalDistanceKm) etc.) so the rendered
  numbers reproduce the web verbatim.

NEVER-HIDE NOTE (ADR-011)
  The web hides chart row 1 (area+bar) when dailyTrend.length <= 2 and each scatter when
  length <= 3. The native port instead ALWAYS renders every ChartContainer and switches it to
  ChartStatus.Empty (common.noData) below the web threshold, so a section is never a blank box —
  strictly stronger than the web while preserving the same data thresholds.

